WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
Narrator: You'll usually get two messages.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.950
Narrator: First, a stand-by message, using a code word you'll learn at your briefing.

3
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:10.300
Narrator: It means get ready - it does NOT mean evacuate.

4
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.200
Narrator: Second, the evacuation message - by radio, on the public address and on the big screens.

5
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.400
Narrator: That means go.

6
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.200
Narrator: If there's no time, the evacuation message may come on its own.

7
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.500
Narrator: When it's over, an all-clear message tells you to return to your post.

8
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.700
Narrator: Keep the code words to yourself - they're there so fans don't panic.

